# Line endings are the repository's, not the checkout machine's.
#
# `npm run check:entities` compares ENTITIES.md byte-for-byte against what
# scripts/entities-md.mjs generates, and the generator writes LF. Without this
# file, a machine with core.autocrlf=true — the Git for Windows default — gets
# CRLF on checkout and the check fails at line 1 on a difference nobody can see,
# reporting two lines that look identical. It bites after any clone, checkout or
# stash, and it would bite a judge cloning this repository to verify it.
#
# `text=auto` still normalizes to LF in the object store, which is what was
# always committed; `eol=lf` is what stops the working tree from diverging.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Anything that is not text is left alone, so nothing is corrupted by
# normalization it should never have had.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.excalidraw binary
